mework.\n    50→ * The renderer is responsible for:\n    51→ * - Converting raw props/slots into a reactive system the framework understands\n    52→ * - Mounting and unmounting component instances\n    53→ * - Applying incremental updates (props, slots, JSON patches) to mounted components\n    54→ * - Server-side rendering (optional)\n    55→ *\n    56→ * ## Lifecycle\n    57→ *\n    58→ * 1. `mount()` is called when the LiveView hook mounts. The renderer should:\n    59→ *    - Create reactive wrappers around props\n    60→ *    - Create slot render functions from HTML strings\n    61→ *    - Mount the framework component into the DOM element\n    62→ *    - Return a `RendererState` that the hook will store\n    63→ *\n    64→ * 2. `updateProps()` / `patchProps()` are called when the LiveView sends updates.\n    65→ *    The renderer must update the reactive props in-place to trigger re-renders.\n    66→ *\n    67→ * 3. `updateSlots()` is called when slot content changes.\n    68→ *\n    69→ * 4. `unmount()` is called when the LiveView hook is destroyed.\n    70→ *\n    71→ * ## Adding a New Framework\n    72→ *\n    73→ * ```ts\n    74→ * import type { FrameworkRenderer } from \"live_vite/renderer\"\n    75→ *\n    76→ * const reactRenderer: FrameworkRenderer = {\n    77→ *   name: \"react\",\n    78→ *   mount(ctx) { ... },\n    79→ *   updateProps(state, newProps) { ... },\n    80→ *   patchProps(state, operations) { ... },\n    81→ *   updateSlots(state, newSlots) { ... },\n    82→ *   unmount(state) { ... },\n    83→ * }\n    84→ * ```\n    85→ */\n    86→export interface FrameworkRenderer<TApp = unknown> {\n    87→  /** Human-readable name for debugging (e.g. \"vue\", \"react\", \"svelte\") */\n    88→  readonly name: string\n    89→\n    90→  /**\n    91→   * Mount a component into the DOM.\n    92→   *\n    93→   * Called during the LiveView hook's `mounted` lifecycle.\n    94→   * The renderer should create a framework app instance, set up reactivity,\n  