{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S9STmiDWqxeTnVHRS1t8QP","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my thorough search of the Astro project, I can provide you with a comprehensive report:\n\n## Search Results Summary\n\nThe Astro project in `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/astro` does **not contain any React hooks related to LiveView, live events, push events, or similar patterns**. \n\n### What I Found Instead\n\nThe Astro project is a meta-framework for building web applications with various frontend frameworks (React, Preact, Vue, Svelte, Solid, etc.). The React components in Astro use standard React patterns:\n\n#### Key React Files Found:\n\n1. **Basic React Counter** (`/home/andre/Documents/scratch/astro/examples/framework-react/src/components/Counter.tsx`)\n   - Uses `useState` hook for local state management\n   - Standard `onClick` event handlers\n\n2. **React Components with Server Actions** (`/home/andre/Documents/scratch/astro/packages/astro/e2e/fixtures/actions-blog/src/components/Like.tsx`)\n   ```tsx\n   import { actions } from 'astro:actions';\n   import { useState } from 'react';\n   \n   export function Like({ postId, initial }: { postId: string; initial: number }) {\n       const [likes, setLikes] = useState(initial);\n       const [pending, setPending] = useState(false);\n       \n       return (\n           <button\n               onClick={async () => {\n                   setPending(true);\n                   setLikes(await actions.blog.like.orThrow({ postId }));\n                   setPending(false);\n               }}\n           >\n               {likes} ❤️\n           </button>\n       );\n   }\n   ```\n\n3. **PostComment Component** (`/home/andre/Documents/scratch/astro/packages/astro/e2e/fixtures/actions-blog/src/components/PostComment.tsx`)\n   - Uses Astro's `actions` API for server communication\n   - Form submission with error handling\n   - No custom LiveView-style hooks\n\n### Key Differences from LiveView Patterns\n\nAstro uses:\n- **`astro:actions`** module for server communication (not `pushEvent`/`handleEvent`)\n- Standard React hooks (`useState`, `useEffect`)\n- Direct `async` function calls in event handlers (not event-based subscription patterns)\n- HTML form submission with `FormData`\n\n### Conclusion\n\nThe Astro project uses a different architectural pattern than Phoenix LiveView. It doesn't have custom hooks like `useLiveEvent`, `useLiveForm`, or `useLiveNavigation`. Instead, it uses Astro Actions for server communication, which is more similar to traditional API endpoint patterns with `fetch`, rather than the real-time event-driven model of Phoenix LiveView.\n\nIf you're looking for LiveView-style React hooks as a reference, they don't exist in this Astro codebase. The LiveVite library in `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue` is actually the implementation that would provide such hooks for React (as noted in the CLAUDE.md about SSR NodeJS and ViteJS modes for React support)."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a5ef2ed (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 39093\ntool_uses: 26\nduration_ms: 36716</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7a5337bc-2da9-4b8b-ba82-bac54b4774d1","uuid":"c531fe03-9b6a-443d-a681-4b82075ab8da","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Search the /home/andre/Documents/scratch/astro directory for any React hooks related to LiveView, live events, push events, or similar patterns. Look for files like useLive.ts, useLiveEvent.ts, or any hook files. Also search for \"useLive\", \"pushEvent\", \"handleEvent\" in tsx/ts files. Show me the relevant code.","agentId":"a5ef2ed","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my thorough search of the Astro project, I can provide you with a comprehensive report:\n\n## Search Results Summary\n\nThe Astro project in `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/astro` does **not contain any React hooks related to LiveView, live events, push events, or similar patterns**. \n\n### What I Found Instead\n\nThe Astro project is a meta-framework for building web applications with various frontend frameworks (React, Preact, Vue, Svelte, Solid, etc.). The React components in Astro use standard React patterns:\n\n#### Key React Files Found:\n\n1. **Basic React Counter** (`/home/andre/Documents/scratch/astro/examples/framework-react/src/components/Counter.tsx`)\n   - Uses `useState` hook for local state management\n   - Standard `onClick` event handlers\n\n2. **React Components with Server Actions** (`/home/andre/Documents/scratch/astro/packages/astro/e2e/fixtures/actions-blog/src/components/Like.tsx`)\n   ```tsx\n   import { actions } from 'astro:actions';\n   import { useState } from 'react';\n   \n   export function Like({ postId, initial }: { postId: string; initial: number }) {\n       const [likes, setLikes] = useState(initial);\n       const [pending, setPending] = useState(false);\n       \n       return (\n           <button\n               onClick={async () => {\n                   setPending(true);\n                   setLikes(await actions.blog.like.orThrow({ postId }));\n                   setPending(false);\n               }}\n           >\n               {likes} ❤️\n           </button>\n       );\n   }\n   ```\n\n3. **PostComment Component** (`/home/andre/Documents/scratch/astro/packages/astro/e2e/fixtures/actions-blog/src/components/PostComment.tsx`)\n   - Uses Astro's `actions` API for server communication\n   - Form submission with error handling\n   - No custom LiveView-style hooks\n\n### Key Differences from LiveView Patterns\n\nAstro uses:\n- **`astro:actions`** module for server communication (not `pushEvent`/`handleEvent`)\n- Standard React hooks (`useState`, `useEffect`)\n- Direct `async` function calls in event handlers (not event-based subscription patterns)\n- HTML form submission with `FormData`\n\n### Conclusion\n\nThe Astro project uses a different architectural pattern than Phoenix LiveView. It doesn't have custom hooks like `useLiveEvent`, `useLiveForm`, or `useLiveNavigation`. Instead, it uses Astro Actions for server communication, which is more similar to traditional API endpoint patterns with `fetch`, rather than the real-time event-driven model of Phoenix LiveView.\n\nIf you're looking for LiveView-style React hooks as a reference, they don't exist in this Astro codebase. The LiveVite library in `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue` is actually the implementation that would provide such hooks for React (as noted in the CLAUDE.md about SSR NodeJS and ViteJS modes for React support)."}],"totalDurationMs":36716,"totalTokens":39093,"totalToolUseCount":26,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1192,"cache_read_input_tokens":37160,"output_tokens":734,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1192,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0}}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01F1FFTmTNedmAdHUS2zCvoE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a clear picture. Let me understand the design:\n\n1. **Vue approach**: `useLiveVite()` uses Vue's `inject()` to get the hook instance, which the Vue renderer provides via `app.provide(liveInjectKey, ctx.hook)`.\n\n2. **React approach**: The React renderer passes `live: ctx.hook` as a prop to the component. So currently React components access it via `props.live`.\n\nFor React, I need to create a proper React context + hooks system similar to Vue's composables. The React renderer currently passes `hook` as a prop (`live`), but a `useLive()` hook via React Context would be more idiomatic. I need to:\n\n1. Create a React context for the live hook\n2. Create a provider component that the React renderer wraps around the user's component\n3. Create `useLive()` and `useLiveEvent()` hooks\n4. Update the React renderer to use the context provider instead of (or in addition to) passing `live` as a prop\n\nLet me check the `LiveHook` / `ViewHook` types to understand the interface."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2676,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1078,"cache_read_input_tokens":42794,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1078},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7a5337bc-2da9-4b8b-ba82-bac54b4774d1","uuid":"84526ef3-752a-4fe2-a780-9f00a3484fd1"}
